DTSTAMP:20260714T030424Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260719T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260719T153000
SUMMARY:Copperhead Trail at Haywood Community College on National Ice Crea
 m Day
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nIt's likely to be hot\, s
 o at the end of the walk we will go get an ice cream together.\n\nTo get t
 o the Copperhead Trail from our start point\, we will go clockwise on the 
 Bobcat Trail\, and then take the Kingfisher Trail to the Copperhead Trail.
  When we intersect with the Millpond Connector\, we will turn left\, finis
 hing the campus loop on the Bobcat Trail. All together\, it isn't over 2 m
 iles. Part of the walk is on pavement\, part on well-groomed trail\, and p
 art on not-as-well groomed trail. There is some small elevation change.\n\
 nAs you enter the campus from Jones Cove Road\, go to the first parking lo
 t on the left. We will gather there and then head out.\n\nBe sure to dress
  for the weather. I'm going to wear tennis shoes\, unless it has rained a 
 lot recently (in which case\, I will wear light hiking boots). I plan to b
 ring one walking stick\, just in case. As always\, you are urged to bring 
 **plenty of water** and a protein snack. Dogs are welcome. Trail strollers
  should not have any problem. There are no bathrooms available on a Sunday
  afternoon\, so take care of such needs before you arrive.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/314928269/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260523T231205Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260523T231205Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
